2.2 Updating An Existing WSL2 Installation
==========================================

The guided installer recompiles the source already present in the
Emacsvox checkout, but it does not fetch newer source itself.  Keep the
current speaking Emacsvox session open while updating.  Run the commands
from ‘M-x shell RET’ in that session, or from another accessible WSL
terminal:

     cd ~/src/emacsvox
     git pull --ff-only
     ./bin/emacsvox-wsl-install --check
     ./bin/emacsvox-wsl-install

   Replace ‘~/src/emacsvox’ if you chose another Linux-filesystem
location.  The fast-forward-only pull does not create a merge commit.
If Git reports local changes, a divergent branch, or another error, stop
and review that checkout; do not reset or discard files merely to
complete an update.

   Rerunning the installer reuses supported Emacs and verified cached
downloads, installs a newly pinned Omnivox release when necessary,
rebuilds Emacsvox byte-code from scratch so files from the previous
source revision cannot survive, and repeats the launch checks.  These
operations change files on disk but do not stop the Emacsvox process
already providing speech.  If the update fails, leave that session
running while using it to inspect the reported error and the named log
file.

   After the installer succeeds and you hear its final check, leave the
old Emacsvox session open and start a second, isolated process from the
updated checkout:

     cd ~/src/emacsvox
     ./bin/emacsvox

   Running both sessions temporarily is deliberate: the old session
remains the known-good source of speech while you test the replacement.
The new process cannot retain Lisp loaded from the previous version.
Confirm that it speaks the ready message and ordinary buffer contents.
In the new session, use ‘M-x emacsvox-speak-version RET’ to hear the
Emacsvox version and ‘M-x tts-speak-version RET’ to hear the live
speech-server version.  Only after these checks pass should you save
work in the old session and exit it.  You can then continue in the
isolated session or start Emacsvox through your normal customized entry
point.  If the new session does not speak, close it but leave the old
session running while you inspect the diagnostic and installer logs.

   For an Emacsvox-only manual update, keep the current session running
and replace the two guided-installer commands after ‘git pull --ff-only’
with:

     make check-emacs
     make bytecode-rebuild
     ./bin/emacsvox --diagnose
     ./bin/emacsvox --check

   All four commands must succeed, and the final check must produce both
its tone and speech, before performing the second-session test above.
This manual route rebuilds Emacsvox but does not download or select a
newly pinned Omnivox release.  When Omnivox also needs to be updated
independently, follow the _Manual Release Installation_ subsection in
*note Installing An Omnivox Windows Release Under WSL2::, then repeat
the diagnostic and audible check above.


