16 Developer And Maintainer Guide
*********************************

This guide is for people changing Emacsvox source, documentation,
integrations, speech-server protocols, build machinery, or release
staging.  It is included at the end of the published manual so that an
installed Info manual and an offline checkout remain complete, but it is
not part of the ordinary installation and use path.

   Before making a governed change, read ‘AGENTS.md’ and every accepted
record in ‘docs/adr/’.  Use the Emacs selected by ‘local.mk’ for
repository checks.  The generated *note Emacsvox Reference Manual:
(emacsvox-reference)Top. is the exact inventory of Lisp commands,
options, and keymaps; the chapters that follow explain contracts and
procedures that cannot be generated from those interfaces.

* Menu:

* Documentation Maintenance::    Author, validate, and publish Emacsvox documentation.
* Speech Server Protocols::      Understand speech-server protocols.
* Integration Maintenance::      Maintain optional integrations and release staging.


